# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Local (non-committed) config overrides — may contain secrets
*.local.json
configs/*.local.json

# Editor/IDE
.idea/
# .vscode/

# Project artefacts kept out of the repo
KORVUN-Documento-Maestro.pdf
# Compiled CLI binary produced by `go build` at the module root.
/korvun

# OS cruft
.DS_Store

# Local SQLite databases (conversation store) and their WAL/SHM sidecars
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Security/CI artefacts generated locally
results.sarif
*.spdx.json

# Release/distribution output (GoReleaser, future packaging)
/dist/

# Frontend tooling (future no-code builder)
node_modules/
frontend/dist/
.gstack/

# GoReleaser build output (ADR-0025, Stage 15)
dist/

# Desktop packaging output (SP7, private-pass lesson 2026-07-25). The compiled
# binary / .app / installer / .dmg land in build/bin/ (the Wails output
# convention, verified at source: `wails build` writes <projectdir>/build/bin/).
# Ignore ONLY the output subtree — the committed scaffold lives under build/
# itself (appicon, darwin/Info.plist + entitlements, windows/installer .nsi),
# which a blanket build/ ignore would wrongly drop. `**/` so it matches the real
# project dir cmd/korvun-desktop/build/bin/ (where main.go lives, so wails builds
# there) as well as any root-level build/bin/.
**/build/bin/

# Builder frontend (ADR-0029, Stage 14 Phase 2b). The real Vite build is
# regenerated fresh (CI never trusts a committed one, §6), but the committed
# placeholder must survive the global dist/ ignore above so //go:embed dist matches
# on a clean clone and a bare `go build` compiles (§4). Re-include the dir, ignore
# its contents, keep only the placeholder.
!web/builder/dist/
web/builder/dist/*
!web/builder/dist/.gitkeep
!web/builder/dist/index.html

# Desktop chrome (SP6a): same stub pattern as the builder — the committed
# placeholder keeps //go:embed all:frontend/dist matching on a clean clone;
# the real bundle comes from `make desktop-frontend` and is never trusted
# from git.
!cmd/korvun-desktop/frontend/dist/
cmd/korvun-desktop/frontend/dist/*
!cmd/korvun-desktop/frontend/dist/.gitkeep
!cmd/korvun-desktop/frontend/dist/index.html

# Obsidian per-machine vault config (Claude Code IDE plugin)
.obsidian/

# Wails runtime JS (frontend/wailsjs/runtime), copied into the frontend by
# `wails build` REGARDLESS of -skipbindings — that flag gates only the generated
# BINDINGS, not the runtime copy (verified on disk after `make desktop`, SP7).
# The Korvun chrome never imports it (it talks to the core via the SP4 fetch
# proxy, not Wails bindings), so it is a pure build artifact — never committed.
cmd/korvun-desktop/frontend/wailsjs/

# graphify knowledge-graph build artifacts (regenerated on commit to master)
graphify-out/

# understand-anything knowledge-graph artifacts (local analysis, regenerated by /understand)
.ua/

# Design mockup drafts (Chano) — deliberately unversioned (SP2 rider)
design-drafts/

# Copilot report mirror at the repo root (a hook re-creates it; canonical
# copy lives in design-drafts/, which is already ignored).
/claude-code-report.md
